When a `beforeRequest` hook returns a `Response` object, it bypasses the entire network request and retry mechanism. The returned `Response` is treated as the final result of the operation.

If the returned `Response` has a non-2xx status code (like 500) and the default `throwHttpErrors: true` option is active, Ky will immediately reject the promise with an `HTTPError`. The retry logic is never initiated.

This behavior is confirmed by the test case `'beforeRequest hook returning non-ok Response does not re-enter retry handling'` in `test/hooks.ts`.

